# Commercial Cleaning

Source: [Commercial Cleaning](https://beachlinecleaners.com/commercial-cleaning/)

Routine cleaning for small offices, professional suites, retail spaces, and shared work areas. We build the checklist around your space, access requirements, and the schedule that works for the business.

## What routine commercial cleaning can include

Choose the tasks your space needs from the routine checklist below.

- Dusting and wiping reachable surfaces in offices, reception areas, conference rooms, and shared spaces
- Restroom cleaning, including toilets, sinks, counters, mirrors, fixtures, and floors
- Breakroom and kitchenette counters, sinks, tables, appliance exteriors, and floors
- Vacuuming carpets and mopping suitable hard-floor surfaces
- Trash removal, with recycling handled according to the arrangement for the property
- Wiping frequently touched surfaces such as door handles and light switches

## Who this is for

Start with the areas that need attention most, then choose a cleaning schedule that fits your working day.

## Options & Add-ons

Need more than routine upkeep? Tell us which of these options would help.

- Recurring weekly, biweekly, or custom schedules by arrangement
- After-hours or weekend visits, subject to availability
- Detail cleaning for baseboards, trim, fixtures, and buildup
- Interior entry-door and other accessible interior glass
- Restocking restroom and breakroom supplies by arrangement

## What affects the price

Custom quote

Commercial quotes are based on the size and type of space, cleaning frequency, number of restrooms and shared areas, requested cleaning hours, and the final checklist. We confirm the scope and price before the first visit.

- Square footage
- Facility type & layout
- Service frequency
- Restrooms & shared areas
- Cleaning hours & access
- Agreed checklist

## Service FAQs

### Do you clean after hours?

After-hours or weekend cleaning can be arranged when availability and building access allow it. Include your preferred cleaning window with the quote request.

### Can we customize the cleaning checklist?

Yes. Commercial service is based on an agreed checklist for your space. Tell us which areas matter most, any tasks that need special attention, and how often you want them handled.

### Do you bring cleaning supplies and equipment?

We bring standard cleaning supplies and equipment for the agreed service. If the property requires specific products or has delicate surfaces, tell us before the first visit.

### How do you handle keys, alarms, or building access?

We work out access before service starts. If the building uses keys, codes, an alarm, a front desk, or another access process, include that when we set up the schedule. Do not send door or alarm codes through the quote form.

### Can I request a one-time commercial clean?

Yes. One-time cleaning can be quoted along with recurring service. Tell us the condition of the space and whether you need routine cleaning or more detailed work so we can price the scope correctly.

